  "question": {
    "text": "For the arrangement in the figure, the particle <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> attached to one end of a string which moves on a horizontal table in a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> (where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> is the length of the string) with the constant angular speed <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></math>. The other end of the string attached to mass <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> which rests on a vertical rod. When the rod collapse, the acceleration of mass <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> at that instant<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0086_8dc0c3d4e8be.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 263px; width: 250px;\" />"
  },
